    "nvda": {
      "question": "What has happened at NVIDIA since its latest filing? Cite dated sources.",
      "answer": "- **NVIDIA (NVDA)—since the February 25, 2026 filing anchor:**\n  - **March 16, 2026 — Samsung Global Newsroom | third_party:** Samsung announced plans to showcase its NVIDIA collaboration at GTC, including accelerated-computing and digital-twin manufacturing applications. The extracted page also describes memory designed for NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform. [W5][W11]\n  - **March 17, 2026 — TSPA Semiconductor/Substack | third_party:** TSPA reported that NVIDIA’s GTC keynote introduced Vera Rubin, Vera CPU and NemoClaw, while previewing the Feynman platform. These are attributed reports of announcements, not independently verified deployment outcomes. [W1]\n  - **August 12, 2026 — Network World | third_party:** Network World’s roundup reported NVIDIA’s cuFile open-sourcing initiative, the Open Secure AI Alliance and a new Spectrum-X networking platform. This is the roundup’s supplied publication date, not a separately verified publication date for each announcement. [W3][W12]\n\n- **Missing outputs:** Dated official NVIDIA releases and developments published after August 12 were not established within the search budget. Returned official pages lacked supplied publication dates; their retrieval freshness does not establish when developments occurred or confirm their claims.\n\nUnresolved outputs:\n- Live search unavailable: account usage verification (usage endpoint HTTP 429); source results retain conservative credit reservations.\n- Dated official NVIDIA releases were not established within the two-search budget; returned official sources lacked published_date.\n- Post–August 12, 2026 developments were not established within the search budget.",
