      "question": "Is the export-control risk in AMD's FY2025 10-K still current? Check for an official update.",
      "answer": "- Filed statement: AMD’s FY2025 10-K, for the year ended December 27, 2025, says certain Instinct and Versal products require export licenses. MI308 sales into China remain dependent on customer demand, China’s import rules and U.S. licenses—even though some licenses had been granted. [S3] [S5]\n- Official update: AMD’s subsequent 10-Q for the quarter ended June 27, 2026, continues to disclose the MI308 licensing restriction and those same conditions on China sales. [W1]\n- Conclusion: Yes—the later official filing confirms that the export-control exposure persists; the licenses do not establish unrestricted market access. This verifies the specific filed statement, not every aspect of current export policy. [W1]\n\nUnresolved outputs:\n- Live search unavailable: account usage verification (usage endpoint HTTP 429); source results retain conservative credit reservations.",
