    "mixed": {
      "question": "Explain Qualcomm's FY2025 revenue change and what has happened since the filing.",
      "answer": "Financial Analysis / Quant:\n- Qualcomm’s FY2025 consolidated revenue increased by $5.322 billion [C1], or 13.66% [C2], from $38.962 billion [F1] to $44.284 billion [F2].\n- Comparison uses original-report US GAAP figures: FY2024 ran September 25, 2023–September 29, 2024 (53 weeks) [F1]; FY2025 ran September 30, 2024–September 28, 2025 (52 weeks) [F2]. No week-count normalization was applied.\n- Supported arithmetic and inputs are complete; growth calculation independently inspected. Verified CSV table and PNG chart are available.\n- Filing explanations and developments since the November 5, 2025 filing [F2] remain with Research and Current Developments, respectively; they are outside this calculation output.\n\nFilings Research:\n- Qualcomm’s FY2025 revenue rose from $38.962 billion [F1] to $44.284 billion [F2], an increase of $5.322 billion [C1], or 13.66% [C2].\n- Growth was primarily driven by QCT, with higher revenue across handsets, IoT and automotive; licensing revenue was broadly unchanged. [S18] [S16]\n- Handsets benefited from higher average selling prices, favorable product mix and higher chipset shipments by certain major manufacturers. Both pricing/mix and shipments benefited from stronger demand for premium-tier Snapdragon platforms in Android devices. [S14] [S16]\n- IoT growth reflected higher shipments across edge networking, consumer and industrial products, partially offset by unfavorable mix. Automotive growth primarily reflected increased shipments associated with new vehicle launches using Snapdragon digital cockpit products. [S16]\n- The comparison uses original-report US GAAP figures: FY2025 covered September 30, 2024–September 28, 2025, or 52 weeks [F2]; FY2024 covered September 25, 2023–September 29, 2024, or 53 weeks [F1]. The supplied growth calculation is not week-count normalized. [C2]\n\nCurrent Developments:\n- **Qualcomm developments published after the November 5, 2025 filing:**\n  - **February 4, 2026 — q4cdn.com | third_party:** Qualcomm’s earnings presentation described the Augentix acquisition as expanding its intelligent-camera capabilities and an expanded Google collaboration on automotive innovation and AI-powered mobility. [W2]\n  - **June 24, 2026 — Qualcomm | official:** Its Investor Day business update emphasized diversification into data centers, industrial AI, robotics and automotive autonomy. These were strategic priorities and forward-looking opportunities, not established outcomes. [W4]\n  - **August 3, 2026 — Futurum | third_party:** Futurum reported that Qualcomm’s Modular acquisition added an open AI software stack for heterogeneous computing across data-center and edge deployments. [W1]\n- **Evidence limits:** Publication dates establish that these sources appeared after the filing; they do not independently verify the claims or establish present status.\n\nUnresolved outputs:\n- Live search unavailable: account usage verification (usage endpoint HTTP 429); source results retain conservative credit reservations.",
